{"Reminder cancellation functions are invoked inside forEach loops without awaiting the returned promises, so handlers can continue before SendGrid/Twilio cancellation or database updates complete, and try/catch only catches synchronous errors": 0.9483080506324768, "deleteScheduledEmailReminder with immediateDelete=true calls SendGrid API to cancel but does NOT delete the reminder from the database, leaving inconsistent state between DB (not cancelled) and SendGrid (cancelled)": 0.9413650035858154, "getBookingToDelete() function does not include workflowReminders in the select clause, causing TypeError when handleCancelBooking.ts tries to iterate over booking.workflowReminders which will be undefined": 0.2095789909362793, "Migration 20260319000000_drop_workflow_tables drops the entire WorkflowReminder table, making all workflow reminder code fail and negating the PR's changes that add the 'cancelled' column": 0.005060245748609304, "requestRescheduleHandler does not cancel workflow reminders from the previous booking before rescheduling, creating a race condition where workflow reminders might still fire after the user requests a reschedule": 0.239787757396698, "Conditional logic changed from (isPhoneNumberNeeded || isSenderIdNeeded) to just isPhoneNumberNeeded, removing isSenderIdNeeded condition which could silently break SMS sender ID functionality": 0.8368897438049316, "deleteScheduledSMSReminder doesn't handle Twilio cancellation failures properly - if referenceId exists but Twilio API throws an error, the catch block returns without deleting the reminder from the database, leaving orphaned records": 0.9318231344223022}